{"title":"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Using_equations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Using equations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a middle-school mentoring program, a number of the sixth graders are paired with a ninth-grade student as a buddy. No ninth grader is assigned more than one sixth-grade buddy. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of all the ninth graders are paired with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of all the sixth graders, what fraction of the total number of sixth and ninth graders have a buddy?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fda518ae91af02c569bf2b78ed5f4f89110bee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{2}{15} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{4}{11} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{11}{30} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{3}{8} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{11}{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Using_equations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Using_equations)\">Solution 1 (Using equations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Using equations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the number of sixth graders be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and the number of ninth graders be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/53768541640035bb5bf7dd1d7e43478bf101f2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{3}=\\frac{2s}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"59\" height=\"37\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ada9ff4f25d3edaa1a60de2cefc2a88698412c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\frac{6s}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />. Since we are trying to find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12aec03643ad0198e5382d7fca7df38b5393c88a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{n}{3}+\\frac{2s}{5}}{n+s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"53\" height=\"42\" />, we can just substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea8a280d80558162d980829098479f74ff60655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6s}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> for  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />  into the equation. We then get a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958e4fb465a227ae9e74a5b5c91c96d5d420dcb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{\\frac{6s}{5}}{3}+\\frac{2s}{5}}{\\frac{6s}{5}+s} = \\frac{\\frac{6s+6s}{15}}{\\frac{11s}{5}} = \\frac{\\frac{4s}{5}}{\\frac{11s}{5}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~\\frac{4}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"274\" height=\"52\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Easy)\">Solution 2 (Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that the minimum number of ninth graders is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, because if there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> then there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ninth-grader with a buddy, which would mean there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40cba44ffc429fc98e11a1605ced22243b655f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> sixth graders, which is impossible (of course unless you really do have half of a person). With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ninth-graders, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them are in the buddy program, so there <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f6b510564528265c42e0ea35c072bebb20c142d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\tfrac{2}{5}}=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"47\" height=\"43\" /> sixth-graders total, two of whom have a buddy. Thus, the desired fraction is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245755f43ce0a8730cd63371d5f4aa49b2cee084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2+2}{5+6}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{4}{11}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"137\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kJAJXJTKjSk\">https://youtu.be/kJAJXJTKjSk</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u3otXEQgsUU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u3otXEQgsUU</a>   ~David\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7md_65nXjTw\">https://youtu.be/7md_65nXjTw</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 8\">2015 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195957\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 167/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3766/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.368      1 -total\n 58.43%    7.226      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 39.65%    4.904      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14451:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195957 and revision id 252716. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}